WEBVTT

NOTE
Automatic English captions. Generated locally and checked with additional audio decodes; not fully audited by listening.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.180
You probably know by now that agents work
better when they have the right context

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:10.300
and instructions. The hard part is giving
them that guidance without stuffing every

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:16.260
prompt full of repetitive details that may
not matter for the current task. That's

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:21.320
what skills are for. A skill is like a
playbook or a manual the agent can pull in

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.040
when it needs it, so the detailed
instructions show up at the right moment

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.700
instead of sitting in the way. Let me show
you how that works.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.640
This is the same agent from before with
its web tools. Ask it to qualify a lead

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.360
and with no method to follow, it just runs
a quick search. So the answer it gives is

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.960
a guess, vague and unsourced.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.760
A skill fixes that. It's a written method
the agent can read, a playbook for how to

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.760
do the job well.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.620
You attach the skill to the agent
alongside the tools it already has.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:09.400
Now, run the same request again. This
time, the agent reaches for the skill mid

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.080
-run, loading it right in the
conversation, the way it would call a

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.360
tool. Following the method, it turns each
claim into a question and pulls a sourced

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.620
answer for every one.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.400
The result is a detailed, cited answer,
where before there was only a guess.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.780
And the playbook never clogs the agent's
context. Only its name and description

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.520
stay in view. And the full method loads
only when the agent decides it's relevant.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.400
You don't even have to write them. Every
integration ships with ready -to -use

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.800
skills that give your agents instant
expertise.
